---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "Create a Windows 11 bootable USB on macOS — Bootable",
  description: "Create Windows 11 USB installer media on Apple Silicon macOS with FAT32, split WIM support, native disk handling, and verification.",
  ogTitle: "Create a Windows 11 bootable USB on macOS",
  ogDescription: "Native disk handling, FAT32 media, split WIM support, and boot-tree checks.",
  ogType: "article",
  current: "guide",
  doc: { label: "Safety", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/docs/safety.md" },
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides.html" }, { label: "Windows USB on macOS" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <article>
        <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Windows installer · macOS</p><h1>Create a Windows 11 USB on macOS.</h1><p class="lede">Bootable uses native macOS disk tools, a fixed root-owned helper, and wimlib to build verified FAT32 installer media.</p></header>
        <div class="guide-body">
          <div class="guide-content">
            <h2 id="support">Current macOS support</h2>
            <p>The alpha supports Apple Silicon. It discovers whole removable devices, excludes the macOS root disk, unmounts the selected target, and writes through its raw device path.</p>
            <p>For Windows installer media, the source ISO is mounted read-only. Bootable creates GPT or MBR FAT32 media with <code>diskutil</code> and copies the validated setup tree.</p>

            <h2 id="requirements">Before you start</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>An Apple Silicon Mac.</li>
              <li>A trusted Windows 11 ISO.</li>
              <li>An expendable USB drive with enough capacity.</li>
              <li><code>wimlib</code> when the ISO contains an oversized WIM or CA 2023 files are requested.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="guide-commands"><pre><code>brew install wimlib
curl -fsSL https://bootable.palash.dev/install.sh | sh -s -- --gui</code></pre></div>
            <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>The alpha is not signed or notarized.</strong> macOS may show a security warning. Review the installer and release SHA-256 file before running it.</p></div>

            <h2 id="helper">Install the protected helper</h2>
            <p>The installer places the fixed helper at <code>/Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/app.bootable.helper</code> after administrator authentication. The desktop app remains unprivileged. Bootable rejects a helper that is not protected by root ownership.</p>

            <h2 id="steps">Create the installer</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>Open the Windows 11 ISO in Bootable.</li>
              <li>Select the USB drive by its physical model and capacity.</li>
              <li>Choose GPT or MBR and any required Windows setup options.</li>
              <li>Review the source, target, operations, dependencies, and permanent erasure.</li>
              <li>Confirm the reviewed plan and authenticate when macOS asks.</li>
              <li>Keep the drive connected through the final boot-tree check.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2 id="verification">What happens after copying</h2>
            <p>Bootable checks the UEFI boot tree, Windows setup payload, split WIM sequence, and FAT32 size rules. Cancellation terminates controlled media tools and marks the drive incomplete so it is not mistaken for finished media.</p>
            <p>The structural check does not guarantee that Windows Setup will complete on every target computer.</p>

            <section class="related-guides"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/verify-bootable-usb">Understand the verification result</a></li><li><a href="/safe-usb-writer">Review the macOS safety boundary</a></li><li><a href="/windows-11-usb-on-linux">Create the same media on Linux</a></li></ul></section>
            <div class="guide-cta"><h2>Install Bootable on macOS</h2><p>The current macOS build supports Apple Silicon.</p><a class="button primary" href="/download">View install commands</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-aside"><strong>On this page</strong><ul><li><a href="#support">macOS support</a></li><li><a href="#requirements">Requirements</a></li><li><a href="#helper">Protected helper</a></li><li><a href="#steps">Create the installer</a></li><li><a href="#verification">Verification</a></li></ul></aside>
        </div>
      </article>
</main>
</Layout>
